#
# Docker build context filter for the root context used by every service that
# builds through openbank-infra/docker/services/standalone-service.Dockerfile.
#
# Without this file, every per-service rebuild streams 900+ MB of context
# (28 × node_modules, all .gradle caches, all .next caches, all docs assets,
# every screenshot in attic/) — observed taking ~140 s just on the upload
# phase and burning the Docker daemon under load.
#
# This is independent of .gitignore: docker buildx ignores .gitignore.

# --- Local build / dependency caches ---
**/build/
**/.gradle/
**/.kotlin/
**/.quarkus/
**/node_modules/
# Also match a node_modules SYMLINK (no trailing slash): host-side generators in
# build-push-admin-ui.sh may symlink openbank-admin-ui/node_modules to a sibling checkout
# so they can `import 'yaml'`. Without this, the symlink leaks into the build context and
# clobbers the container's own node_modules → `sh: next: not found` at `npm run build`.
**/node_modules
**/.next/
**/.turbo/
**/.npm/
**/.yarn/
**/dist/
**/.cache/
.gradle/
# Read-only private mobile-app checkout used only by the deploy-time client-evidence
# collector. It must never become part of the public admin-ui build context or image.
/.app-src/

# --- Reports / artefacts ---
**/build/reports/
**/coverage/
# Gradle JUnit XML output — scope to build/ so it does NOT also nuke the
# admin-ui API route at src/app/api/test-results/ (a bare `**/test-results/`
# glob matched that route dir, excluding it from the image → route absent →
# Next served a bare 404 for /api/test-results).
**/build/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
**/allure-results/
**/allure-report/

# --- IDE / editor / tooling ---
.idea/
.vscode/
.history/
.claude/
.cursor/
.sisyphus/
.aider*
.continue/
*.iml

# --- VCS ---
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.dockerignore

# --- OS / temp ---
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.tmp
*.bak

# --- Docs / large assets / planned services ---
docs/
attic/
*.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!LICENSE
# Per-service docs MUST stay in context — the admin-ui Dockerfile bundles
# every openbank-<svc>/docs/ tree into a read-only artifact at image build
# (see openbank-admin-ui/Dockerfile docs-collector stage). The container has
# zero host-fs view at runtime; docs are served from the immutable bundle.
!openbank-*/docs
!openbank-*/docs/**
# Per-service release-please CHANGELOG.md MUST stay in context — the admin-ui
# Dockerfile bundles every openbank-<svc>/CHANGELOG.md into a read-only artifact
# (changelog-collector stage) so /docs/changelog and /docs/release-notes render
# version history offline (private repo, no pod token). Overrides the *.md exclude.
!openbank-*/CHANGELOG.md
# Governance corpora MUST stay in context — the admin-ui Dockerfile bundles
# docs/adr + docs/threat-models into a read-only artifact at image build (see
# openbank-admin-ui/Dockerfile governance-collector stage). Same image-baked
# pattern as per-service docs above; re-include overrides the docs/ + *.md
# exclusions for these two trees only.
!docs/adr
!docs/adr/**
!docs/threat-models
!docs/threat-models/**
!docs/agents
!docs/agents/**
# The ADR-0148 prompt registry (registry.yaml + one *.md per registered prompt) is bundled by the
# same stage for the ADR-0285 Communication Studio. Only the *.md files need re-including —
# registry.yaml is a .yaml and was never excluded — but naming the whole tree keeps the rule
# readable and matches how the collector copies it.
!openbank-libs/governance/prompts
!openbank-libs/governance/prompts/**

# Per-service CycloneDX SBOMs (generated by `./gradlew sbomAll`). Bundled
# into the admin-ui image by the sbom-collector stage.
# NOTE: Docker .dockerignore cannot re-include a file whose parent directory
# was already excluded by an earlier rule. `!openbank-*/build` was previously
# used here, but it re-included the ENTIRE build/ tree (~400MB × 30 services
# = ~12GB extra context). The sbom-collector stage in the Dockerfile handles
# 0 bom.json files gracefully. SBOM injection must be done by pre-staging
# the files to a flat directory before the docker build (tracked separately).
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.pdf
UI.png

# --- Logs ---
*.log
**/*.log
logs/

# --- Test container junk ---
pgdata/
postgres-data/
kafka-data/
valkey-data/

# --- Secrets — belt and braces alongside .gitignore ---
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
*.kdbx
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
secrets/
credentials/

# --- Per-service tests (not needed for production image build) ---
**/src/test/

# --- Other services NOT being built ---
# Each per-service build only needs openbank-libs + its own dir, so we keep
# the include-set tight at the build args level (SERVICE_DIR). This file
# does not exclude per-service code because the build needs at least the
# target service's source tree. The big win above is .gradle / .next / docs.
